<%# The prompt is the reader's own words, so it is drawn as a bubble of its own.
    `text` is nil when the history already holds this prompt — a page opened
    while the turn runs draws it from the transcript instead, and two bubbles
    for one prompt is exactly the double render this avoids. -%>
<% if text -%>
<div class="msg user">
  <div class="bubble text"><span class="sr-only"><%= h(I18n.t("web.message.you")) %></span><%= fmt_prompt(text) %></div>
</div>
<% end -%>

<div class="turn"
     hx-ext="sse"
     sse-connect="/turns/<%= h(turn.id) %>/stream<%= h(token_query) %>"
     sse-close="done"
     aria-live="polite"
     x-init="$store.turn.active = '<%= turn.id %>'">
  <%# The id is what a row added at the end is appended to; the rows inside
      carry ids of their own (see View#item_attrs) so one of them can be
      replaced without touching its neighbours. -%>
  <div class="turn-body" id="t-<%= h(turn.id) %>-body" sse-swap="turn"><%= timeline(turn) %></div>
  <%# Where a row that moved arrives. The payload is plain rows: the slot points
      at the timeline's container and appends them, so a row that has no id of
      its own (a diff, a mid-turn message) lands in place like any other. Rows
      that change or leave still carry hx-swap-oob and are taken out of the
      payload before this append runs; this slot then stays empty. -%>
  <div class="turn-patch" sse-swap="turn-patch" hx-target="#t-<%= h(turn.id) %>-body"
       hx-swap="beforeend" hidden></div>
  <%# An ask that was already waiting when the page was refreshed is drawn
      here: its event has long been in the log the stream no longer replays, so
      leaving the slot empty would strand a turn behind a question nobody can
      see. -%>
  <div class="ask" sse-swap="ask"><%= View.render("_ask", prompt: turn.ask_prompt, turn_id: turn.id) %></div>
  <div class="notice" sse-swap="notice"></div>
  <%# Where the status row's out-of-band swap arrives. The payload carries
      hx-swap-oob, so htmx applies it to #usage and this slot stays empty. -%>
  <div class="status-slot" sse-swap="usage" hidden></div>
  <%# Same for the sidebar and the header: the conversation gains its name when
      this turn is written to disk. -%>
  <div class="sidebar-slot" sse-swap="sidebar" hidden></div>
</div>
